findings.description:
v1 needs one transition (`pre-advance`, reviewType `code`), one threshold, and an unknown policy. The doc also adds:
- a nested `[workflow.review_gates]` table with four transitions, three of them unwired (see above);
- `pre-slice-plan` config for a transition the doc itself defers;
- `score`, read and stored with no consumer and no defined storage location;
- `criteria` and `provenance`, carried "as opaque fields with no v1 consumer";
- renumbering the full `getNext` cascade in slice 1, which has no gate logic. The stated reason is weak: `getNext` already uses fractional labels (`Priority 2.5`, `WorkflowNavigator.ts:187`) and `FR-3b` (`:409`).

CF's CLAUDE.md says to always resist adding complexity. Ship `review_enabled`, `review_threshold`, `review_unknown_as`, and the `pre-advance` transition. Defer the rest.
